THIRD-PARTY NOTICES FOR REN
============================
Generated from origin/main by the P0 commercial-dependency/license-audit
lane (engineering half). It is an INVENTORY, not a EULA: it records what
Ren ships or downloads, under which upstream license, and the plain
commercial-use determination for each. Writing the product EULA is a
separate captain's decision and is NOT done here.

How to read a row
-----------------
  component   : what it is
  pin         : the version or revision Ren resolves (file that states it)
  source      : upstream project / download origin
  license     : upstream license of record
  fetched     : shipped-in-repo | pip-install | downloaded-at-install |
                downloaded-at-first-use | external-prerequisite
  commercial  : one of
      ok                  - permissive terms, commercial use allowed
      ok-with-attribution - commercial use allowed with attribution/notice
      needs-paid-license  - commercial use requires a bought license
      not-permitted       - terms forbid the product use; do not ship
  hash-verified : yes | no - whether the fetch is checksum/signature
                checked before use (the download-pinning lane owns
                closing the "no" rows; this file records them).

Maintenance rule: adding a dependency, model, binary, font or asset
requires adding its row here in the same change. Transitive pip
dependencies are NOT enumerated row by row; they are pinned in
requirements/lock/macos-arm64-py312.txt (scripts/lock_python_env.sh),
which is the record of what was measured.

